index 0ce6e8d..5d73d1f 100644
--- a/docs/decisions/0319-cows.md
+++ b/docs/decisions/0319-cows.md
@@ -80,3 +80,20 @@ callers check strings, slices, fixed arrays and generic Clone payloads; negative
 assignments must fail. Runtime assertions check the tag, borrowed buffer identity
 and an owned mutation leaving the input unchanged. The two mutations remove
 recognition or associated-field normalization and must both be caught.
+
+## Amendment: generic AsRef and Borrow read the payload (2026-11-14, #1481)
+
+Std's AsRef<B> and Borrow<B> for Cow<B> now receive dictionaries whose
+method reads the same payload expression that Cow's Deref owner supplies.
+The target must equal that owner's borrowed type: Borrow<Cow<B>> remains
+the blanket self-borrow and returns the enum itself. No tag or positional
+field spelling is reconstructed by dictionaries.
+
+This lifts a refusal without changing Cow's representation, ADR 0262 case A.
+The native corpus comparison covers both variants, strings, slices, fixed
+arrays and paths, an owned mutation leaving the borrowed input unchanged,
+fixed-array identity, and borrowing a Cow as itself. Mutations remove the
+dictionary or return the enum instead of its payload. Borrow<Cow<B>> is
+covered by the native comparison as well; rustc's valid std impl selection
+and the existing self-borrow owner already ensure its target, so ignoring
+the redundant target guard at this later branch is an equivalent mutation.
